# === Privacy: never commit instance data =====================================
# See docs/17-privacy.md. This repository is public: it documents a product,
# never its owner. Anything describing a real backlog, goal or workspace stays
# out of git and lives in the database instead.
#
# NOTE: a '#' only starts a comment at the START of a line. A trailing comment
# becomes part of the pattern and silently disables it, so keep comments above
# the patterns they describe. Verify with: git check-ignore -v <path>

# real areas, weights, tool mappings, external IDs
seed/
# local overrides of any committed config
*.local.*
# personal supplement to the privacy deny-list
.github/privacy-denylist.local.txt
# private siblings of journal entries
*-private.md
docs/50-journal/*-private.md
# exports and screenshots of the live instance
exports/
screenshots/
*.dump
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# === Secrets =================================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

